.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4743:    12	[ADR-0080](0080-signal-intelligence-architecture.md) established the signal bus as the backbone of DailyOS intelligence: events fire, listeners react, Bayesian weights update, briefings recompute. It was designed when signals operated at entity granularity — "this account changed," "this person's title moved." Three in-flight changes break that granularity model:
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4746:    15	2. **Ability-output events.** [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) makes every capability a named, versioned ability producing an `AbilityOutput<T>`. Each output is cache-keyed and invalidation-tracked. "This output changed" is a new event class operating at ability-output granularity.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4752:    21	- **Depth-limited drops.** The original invalidation design capped propagation depth and dropped signals past the cap to avoid runaway cascades. That is correctness-unsafe — a dropped invalidation leaves briefings, scores, and claims silently stale. The adversarial review flagged this.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4766:    35	| Ability output | `AbilityOutputChanged { ability_name, output_id }`, `AbilityOutputInvalidated` | 10³ / day |
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4787:    56	- **PropagateAsync { coalesce }** — emitted to the event log, an invalidation job is enqueued for each affected output. If `coalesce = true`, jobs for the same `(SignalType, EntityId)` collapse within a configurable window. Example: `EntityUpdated { coalesce: true }`, `ClaimTrustChanged { coalesce: true }`, `AbilityOutputChanged { coalesce: true }`.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4804:    73	    (SignalType::AbilityOutputChanged,  PropagationPolicy::PropagateAsync { coalesce: true }),
