.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1741:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:8693:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:3201:.docs/strategy/2026-04-20-v1.4.0-architectural-strategy.md:136:**Every output is provenanced, fingerprinted, and scored.** [ADR-0105](../decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) makes `Provenance` envelope mandatory on every `AbilityOutput<T>` — identity, temporal context, source attribution, composition tree, field-level attribution, trust assessment. [ADR-0106](../decisions/0106-prompt-fingerprinting-and-provider-interface.md) extends the provider interface to return metadata enabling canonical prompt hashing — replay, regression classification, and prompt-vs-input fault isolation all become possible. [ADR-0114](../decisions/0114-scoring-unification.md) consolidates scoring primitives scattered across `signals/bus.rs`, `signals/decay.rs`, `signals/fusion.rs`, and `intelligence/health_scoring.rs` into a single pure-function `scoring::factors` module. Trust Compiler (DOS-5) and health scoring consume the same primitives.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1888:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/DOS-210.md:19:- Companion: DOS-211 (Provenance) — abilities produce `AbilityOutput<T>` which requires Provenance.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1898:.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-299-plan.md:61:Intelligence Loop check: `source_asof` feeds trust freshness and suppression/tombstone resurrection, not direct signals; it can influence health only through Trust Compiler consumers; it belongs in prep/intel context only as provenance metadata; briefing callouts should consume claim/trust state, not raw timestamp heuristics; user feedback remains claim-level.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1931:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:390:.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-211-plan.md:9:DOS-211 creates the provenance substrate every ability returns through `AbilityOutput<T>`. The Linear contract is explicit: "Implement the `Provenance` envelope shape, `TrustAssessment`, composition merge semantics, and `ProvenanceBuilder` helper. Every ability output is wrapped in `AbilityOutput<T>` with provenance." It also says the builder "fails at build time if any output field lacks attribution", `sources[]` is "own direct only", `children[]` carries transitive sources, and "Stable `composition_id` per declared `composes` entry (not positional `child_idx`)."
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1934:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:393:.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-211-plan.md:22:- `envelope.rs` - `Provenance`, `ComposedProvenance`, `InputsSnapshot`, `ProvenanceWarning`, `AbilityOutput<T>` if W3-A has not already supplied it.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1939:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:398:.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-211-plan.md:35:Define `FieldAttribution` with `subject: SubjectAttribution`, `derivation: DerivationKind`, source refs, confidence, and optional `SanitizedExplanation`. `ProvenanceBuilder::finalize<T: Serialize>` serializes the domain output to `serde_json::Value`, expands expected JSON-pointer leaf paths, applies any subtree helpers to concrete leaves, and rejects missing attribution before returning `AbilityOutput<T>`. Direct projections use `pass_through()` to auto-fill field attributions. LLM synthesis requires source refs. Declared confidence requires a sanitized explanation.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1942:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:402:.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-211-plan.md:89:Intelligence Loop check: no new schema write path, signal type, health-scoring rule, briefing surface, or feedback UI is introduced. Provenance is the substrate that later claims/feedback/trust work consumes. Fixtures must use synthetic IDs and generic entity names only. Clippy budget is zero new warnings; schema tests must run under the existing `mcp` feature rather than adding a new dependency.
