.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:3528:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:4889:   298	**Rule 5 — Every ability output carries provenance via `AbilityOutput<T>`.**  
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:3549:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:5083:+DOS-211 creates the provenance substrate every ability returns through `AbilityOutput<T>`. The Linear contract is explicit: "Implement the `Provenance` envelope shape, `TrustAssessment`, composition merge semantics, and `ProvenanceBuilder` helper. Every ability output is wrapped in `AbilityOutput<T>` with provenance." It also says the builder "fails at build time if any output field lacks attribution", `sources[]` is "own direct only", `children[]` carries transitive sources, and "Stable `composition_id` per declared `composes` entry (not positional `child_idx`)."
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:3550:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:5085:+The load-bearing ADR pins are ADR-0105 envelope fields at `.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:24-58`, trust shape at `:106-158`, source attribution at `:165-195`, field attribution at `:206-241`, composition at `:257-266`, builder behavior at `:305-311`, and size budget at `:331-333`. ADR-0102 requires `AbilityOutput<T>` to carry provenance exactly once (`.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:166-179`, `:298-305`) and makes Transform output untrusted for mutation authorization (`:313-323`).
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:3555:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:5099:+Define `FieldAttribution` with `subject: SubjectAttribution`, `derivation: DerivationKind`, source refs, confidence, and optional `SanitizedExplanation`. `ProvenanceBuilder::finalize<T: Serialize>` serializes the domain output to `serde_json::Value`, expands expected JSON-pointer leaf paths, applies any subtree helpers to concrete leaves, and rejects missing attribution before returning `AbilityOutput<T>`. Direct projections use `pass_through()` to auto-fill field attributions. LLM synthesis requires source refs. Declared confidence requires a sanitized explanation.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:3561:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:5133:+Intelligence Loop check: no new schema write path, signal type, health-scoring rule, briefing surface, or feedback UI is introduced. Provenance is the substrate that later claims/feedback/trust work consumes. Fixtures must use synthetic IDs and generic entity names only. Clippy budget is zero new warnings; schema tests must run under the existing `mcp` feature rather than adding a new dependency.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:3563:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:5143:+Missing attribution, invalid subject fit, invalid composition refs, or bad declared confidence are hard finalize errors and return no `AbilityOutput<T>`. Unknown source timestamps are not hard errors; they produce `SourceTimestampUnknown` warnings per ADR-0105 (`.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:401-420`). Oversized provenance degrades by eliding deepest children; if still over 1MB, finalize fails so a raw oversize tree never leaves the ability.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:3567:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:5175:+DOS-211 creates the provenance substrate every ability returns through `AbilityOutput<T>`. The Linear contract is explicit: "Implement the `Provenance` envelope shape, `TrustAssessment`, composition merge semantics, and `ProvenanceBuilder` helper. Every ability output is wrapped in `AbilityOutput<T>` with provenance." It also says the builder "fails at build time if any output field lacks attribution", `sources[]` is "own direct only", `children[]` carries transitive sources, and "Stable `composition_id` per declared `composes` entry (not positional `child_idx`)."
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:3568:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:5177:+The load-bearing ADR pins are ADR-0105 envelope fields at `.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:24-58`, trust shape at `:106-158`, source attribution at `:165-195`, field attribution at `:206-241`, composition at `:257-266`, builder behavior at `:305-311`, and size budget at `:331-333`. ADR-0102 requires `AbilityOutput<T>` to carry provenance exactly once (`.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:166-179`, `:298-305`) and makes Transform output untrusted for mutation authorization (`:313-323`).
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:3573:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:5191:+Define `FieldAttribution` with `subject: SubjectAttribution`, `derivation: DerivationKind`, source refs, confidence, and optional `SanitizedExplanation`. `ProvenanceBuilder::finalize<T: Serialize>` serializes the domain output to `serde_json::Value`, expands expected JSON-pointer leaf paths, applies any subtree helpers to concrete leaves, and rejects missing attribution before returning `AbilityOutput<T>`. Direct projections use `pass_through()` to auto-fill field attributions. LLM synthesis requires source refs. Declared confidence requires a sanitized explanation.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:3579:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:5225:+Intelligence Loop check: no new schema write path, signal type, health-scoring rule, briefing surface, or feedback UI is introduced. Provenance is the substrate that later claims/feedback/trust work consumes. Fixtures must use synthetic IDs and generic entity names only. Clippy budget is zero new warnings; schema tests must run under the existing `mcp` feature rather than adding a new dependency.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:3581:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:5235:+Missing attribution, invalid subject fit, invalid composition refs, or bad declared confidence are hard finalize errors and return no `AbilityOutput<T>`. Unknown source timestamps are not hard errors; they produce `SourceTimestampUnknown` warnings per ADR-0105 (`.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:401-420`). Oversized provenance degrades by eliding deepest children; if still over 1MB, finalize fails so a raw oversize tree never leaves the ability.
