.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14487:1. [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) makes every capability a typed, versioned ability. Many of those are Transform abilities that produce claims. The product will ship with multiple ability authors — `prepare_meeting`, `detect_risk_shift`, `generate_weekly_narrative`, future MCP agents — each asserting claims into the same substrate.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14491:Underneath these three is a harder question the substrate as drafted does not answer: **who is allowed to commit a claim, and when does a claim become load-bearing versus merely under consideration?** Today the answer is implicit: whoever writes it. That works when DailyOS is one engineer's enrichment pipeline. It stops working the moment an LLM-backed agent tries to assert "the champion is departing" based on a faint signal, and the briefing tomorrow morning treats that as ground truth.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14508:| `agent:<name>:<version>` | `agent:prepare_meeting:1.3` | `agent:detect_risk_shift:2.1` | LLM-backed or mixed-mode DailyOS ability producing claims |
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14524:| `committed` | Claim is authoritative. Live in briefings, MCP, chat. | Included in default reads. |
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14563:Claims that do not pass the gate transition to `proposed` and become visible in the Analysis Inbox (v1.5.0 surface). They do not appear in briefings, MCP responses, or any default-read surface.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14569:- **Transform abilities** produce `AbilityOutput<ClaimProposal>` — synthesized assertions with full provenance, but no side effect on `intelligence_claims`.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14625:Version bumps reset the ledger: `agent:prepare_meeting:1.3` and `agent:prepare_meeting:1.4` are different actors. Rationale: a prompt or logic change can materially change behavior; we don't inherit credit or blame across versions.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14635:e.g., `agent:prepare_meeting:1.3-p2.1`. A prompt edit bumps `prompt_template_version`, which changes the composite ledger key, which triggers trust warming on the new key per R1.4. This preserves the intent that prompt changes reset trust without abusing `ability_version` semantics.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14698:     9	DOS-211 creates the provenance substrate every ability returns through `AbilityOutput<T>`. The Linear contract is explicit: "Implement the `Provenance` envelope shape, `TrustAssessment`, composition merge semantics, and `ProvenanceBuilder` helper. Every ability output is wrapped in `AbilityOutput<T>` with provenance." It also says the builder "fails at build time if any output field lacks attribution", `sources[]` is "own direct only", `children[]` carries transitive sources, and "Stable `composition_id` per declared `composes` entry (not positional `child_idx`)."
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14700:    11	The load-bearing ADR pins are ADR-0105 envelope fields at `.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:24-58`, trust shape at `:106-158`, source attribution at `:165-195`, field attribution at `:206-241`, composition at `:257-266`, builder behavior at `:305-311`, and size budget at `:331-333`. ADR-0102 requires `AbilityOutput<T>` to carry provenance exactly once (`.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:166-179`, `:298-305`) and makes Transform output untrusted for mutation authorization (`:313-323`).
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14711:    22	- `envelope.rs` - `Provenance`, `ComposedProvenance`, `InputsSnapshot`, `ProvenanceWarning`, `AbilityOutput<T>` if W3-A has not already supplied it.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14724:    35	Define `FieldAttribution` with `subject: SubjectAttribution`, `derivation: DerivationKind`, source refs, confidence, and optional `SanitizedExplanation`. `ProvenanceBuilder::finalize<T: Serialize>` serializes the domain output to `serde_json::Value`, expands expected JSON-pointer leaf paths, applies any subtree helpers to concrete leaves, and rejects missing attribution before returning `AbilityOutput<T>`. Direct projections use `pass_through()` to auto-fill field attributions. LLM synthesis requires source refs. Declared confidence requires a sanitized explanation.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14732:    43	5. `finalize(data)` validates coverage, computes trust, applies size policy, and wraps the result in `AbilityOutput<T>`.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14778:    89	Intelligence Loop check: no new schema write path, signal type, health-scoring rule, briefing surface, or feedback UI is introduced. Provenance is the substrate that later claims/feedback/trust work consumes. Fixtures must use synthetic IDs and generic entity names only. Clippy budget is zero new warnings; schema tests must run under the existing `mcp` feature rather than adding a new dependency.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14792:   103	Missing attribution, invalid subject fit, invalid composition refs, or bad declared confidence are hard finalize errors and return no `AbilityOutput<T>`. Unknown source timestamps are not hard errors; they produce `SourceTimestampUnknown` warnings per ADR-0105 (`.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:401-420`). Implausible timestamps are carried as warnings for DOS-299 freshness handling; W3-B does not quarantine or migrate data.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14836:    24	Create `src-tauri/src/abilities/mod.rs` as the module root, `src-tauri/src/abilities/registry.rs` as W3-A's owned substrate, and add `pub mod abilities;` beside `services`/`signals` in `src-tauri/src/lib.rs:66-67`. `registry.rs` owns `AbilityCategory`, `Actor`, `AbilityPolicy`, `AbilityDescriptor`, `AbilityContext`, `ConfirmationToken`, `AbilityError`, `AbilityResult<T>`, erased wrapper types, `AbilityRegistry`, registry validation, actor filtering, invocation methods, signal-policy metadata, and doc rendering. `AbilityOutput<T>` is the ADR-0102 return wrapper, but its provenance field is supplied by W3-B's `src-tauri/src/abilities/provenance/`; W3-A and W3-B must merge through an integration branch if neither branch wants a temporary stub.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14862:    50	Signal policy: include descriptor fields now, but do not implement durable invalidation. Linear's DOS-210 comment requires per-ability emit-on-output-change declarations; ADR-0115 defines `AbilityOutputChanged` as ability-output granularity (`.docs/decisions/0115-signal-granularity-audit.md:32-39`) and `PropagateAsync { coalesce: true }` as its policy (`:54-57`). ADR-0115 R1.1/R1.3 says typed `SignalType` and function-form policy registry are prerequisites (`:224-234`, `:249-269`), so DOS-210 records metadata and leaves emission wiring to the signal-policy issue.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14884:    72	Services-only mutations are preserved: abilities compose services and never write DB/file/signal state directly. The macro denies detected service mutators in Read/Transform, and ServiceContext denies writes in non-Live modes. Intelligence Loop check: no new signal type is emitted by W3-A; no health scoring rule changes; no intel context builder migration; no briefing callout; no feedback hook. Only signal-policy metadata is recorded.
.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-217.log:14894:    82	DOS-211 owns `src-tauri/src/abilities/provenance/`. W3-A should not define final provenance internals; it references W3-B's `Provenance` and enforces the `AbilityOutput<T>` envelope once both branches are integrated.
